  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude). This brick's download stage is UNCONFIGURED: the FTP base URL is an empty string ('export ftpbase=\"\"'), the repo is a single initial commit from the brick-template with an unedited README and no dvc.lock outputs or .bb metadata. There is no verifiable evidence of what data it actually downloads. The name 'openfda-kg' and the generic csv2parquet build suggest a knowledge graph derived from openFDA (which is CC0 / public domain, and would make it open/permitted), but this cannot be confirmed from the repository, so it is conservatively classed unknown / commercial unknown. HUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED: identify the real upstream source (the empty ftpbase must be filled in); if it is confirmed to be openFDA data, this can be upgraded to open / CC0 / commercial-use permitted.",
